      "writtenOn": "2019-08-21T21:16:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "why?  if it only requests 1.5A, can\u0027t we treat it the same as non-pd devices for the purposes of distributing power?\n\nsimilarly, if it requests 3A for a while, then re-requests only 1.5A since it doesn\u0027t need it, it would be great to reallocate the power to the 4th device (the tablet).\n\nwe don\u0027t *have* to give 3A back to the non-PD devices, but it would be good to at least redistribute amongst PD-capable devices.\n\nI suspect we\u0027ll ultimately have two bits (PD/non-PD, \u003e1.5A/1.5A) per port along with the order of connection going into this policy algorithm, and a simple priority selection that picks who gets 3A, run each time a state changes.  So the above behavior would just naturally come through.\n\nWe can complicate things if we consider that PD sources and PD devices can advertise and request a range of currents (not just 1.5A/3A), but there\u0027s diminishing returns there...",
